$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The reaction was set up in a nitrogen-filled glovebox. A reaction tube
(Fisher scientific 20 × 125 mm, Cat. No. 1495937A) was charged with
pyridone bromide S09 (210 mg, 0.642 mmol, 1.00 equiv.),11
2-bromophenylboronic acid (1.29 g, 6.42 mmol, 10.0 equiv.),
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (74.2 mg, 0.0642 mmol, 0.100
equiv.), copper(I) iodide (30.5 mg, 0.160 mmol, 0.25 equiv.), and
potassium carbonate (1.06 g, 7.70 mmol, 12.0 equiv.). The mixture was
suspended in 1,2-dimethoxyethane (2 mL) and the tube was sealed with a
Teflon cap (Thermo Scientific SPTA SPTA PTFE/SIL F/18-400 10, Cat. No.
03394B). The reaction vessel was removed from the glovebox and placed in
an oil bath that had been pre-heated to 100 °C. After stirring vigorously
for 12 h, the mixture was cooled to room temperature and quenched with
water (10 mL). The aqueous phase was extracted with ethyl acetate (20 mL
× 3) and the combined organic phases were dried over magnesium sulfate,
filtered, and concentrated. The crude product was purified by silica gel
column chromatography (ethyl acetate/hexanes = 1/2 to 1/1.5). The title
compound as a white foam (197 mg, 76%). Melting point: decomposed above
80 °C. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.59 (ddd, J= 5, 2, 1 Hz, 1H), 8.32 (d,
J = 3 Hz, 1H), 8.11 (d, J = 3 Hz, 1H), 7.72 (td, J = 8, 2 Hz, 1H), 7.67
(dd, J = 8, 1 Hz, 1H), 7.56 (dt, J = 8, 1 Hz, 1H), 7.41-7.54 (m, 6H),
7.36 (td, J = 8, 1 Hz, 1H), 7.18- 7.24 (m, 2H) ppm; 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 160.5, 153.5, 149.9, 141.3, 138.5, 137.8, 137.3, 137.2, 133.1,
132.7, 131.9, 129.6, 129.4, 128.8, 127.4, 126.9, 124.0, 122.1, 118.8,
118.0 ppm. IR: 3053, 1657, 1618, 1583, 1567, 1547, 1324, 1270, 1015, 873,
783, 747, 693 cm-1. HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd. for C22H16BrN2O [M+H+]:
403.0441; found 403.0440.
