$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A dry flask was charged with S5 (0.5 mmol),
phenylboronic acid (91.4 mg, 0.75 mmol) and Na2CO3 (160 mg, 1.5 mmol),
and toluene (3 mL) and H2O (2 mL) were added. The mixture was degassed
under argon for 20 min, and Pd(PPh3)4 (29 mg, 0.025 mmol) was added. The
mixture was heated to 80 °C overnight. H2O (30 mL) was added, and the
mixture was extracted with Et2O (40 mL × 2). The combined organic layers
were dried over anhydrous MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The
residue was purified by flash column chromatography to give 1p or 1z. 1z:
Yield 71%; yellow oil. analytical TLC (silica gel 60), 25% EtOAc in
n-hexane, R f = 0.40; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.85-7.70 (m, 1H),
7.55-7.41 (m, 2H), 7.32-7.24 (m, 6H), 7.17-7.06 (m, 1H), 5.50 (s, 1H),
4.91 (s, 1H), 3.79 (s, 2H), 2.05 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
168.5, 146.1, 140.5, 135.9, 130.7, 128.5, 128.0, 127.4, 125.9, 125.5,
124.3, 114.3, 38.0, 24.1; IR (CHCl3) 3414, 3007, 2927, 1683, 1516, 1452,
908 cm-1; LRMS (EI, 20 eV) m/z 251 (M+, 15), 132 (100); HRMS (EI) for
C17H17NO (M+): calcd 251.1310, found 251.1306.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
